description: "\"progression[19]: Observe,→,Understand,→,Explain,→,Apply,→,Analyze,→,Evaluate,→,Design,→,Optimize,→,Teach,→,Innovate dependencies[15]: Explain,→,Understand,Design,→,Analyze,Optimize,→,Measure,Debug,→,Analyze,Architect,→,Design validation[5]: measurable,observable,teachable,transferable,composable requirements[4]: primary_capability,secondary_capabilities,capability_level,prerequisite_capabilities success[2]: Every knowledge object teaches at least one engineering capability.,Every capability maps to measurable engineering behaviour. guarantees[6]: Language Independent,Framework Independent,Domain Independent,Technology Independent,Graph Native,Extensible\""
spec:
  id: capabilities
  version: 1.0.0
  status: stable
  priority: critical
  module: Ontology
  compiler_stage: Knowledge Representation
  description: "\"\\\"Defines the complete Engineering Capability Ontology. Capabilities represent what an engineer can DO with knowledge. Every Engineering Knowledge Record, Engineering Episode, Artifact, Repository, and Engineering World must reference one or more capabilities. Capabilities are independent from programming languages, frameworks and technologies.\\\"\""
purpose: Represent engineering competence rather than engineering information.
levels:
  L0: Awareness
  L1: Understanding
  L2: Application
  L3: Independent Execution
  L4: Optimization
  L5: Expert Reasoning
  L6: Innovation
future:
  unlimited_capabilities: true
  capability_graph: true
  adaptive_curriculum: true
  competency_tracking: true
